post_install() {
    cat <<'EOF'

  silere is installed at /usr/share/silere-shell

  try it first:  silere try     (in a window, changing nothing)
  start it:      silere-shell
  check it:      silere doctor
  autostart:     add this to your ~/.config/hypr/hyprland.lua:
                   hl.on("hyprland.start", function() hl.exec_cmd("silere-shell") end)
                 or `spawn-at-startup "silere-shell"` to your niri config

  click the active workspace to open the menu and settings,
  or bind it: qs ipc -p /usr/share/silere-shell/shell.qml call menu toggle

  wallpaper colours need a one-time matugen setup:
    bash /usr/share/silere-shell/scripts/install.sh --repair-matugen

  it writes only Silere's own template and its marked block in
  ~/.config/matugen/config.toml, and refuses an entry it does not own.
  run matugen once after that. the palette is user-writable and reloads
  live; without it Silere uses its bundled fallback. the same command is
  behind Settings > System > Maintenance.

  cava needs no setup: Silere supplies a temporary profile while its audio
  visualizer is visible and never changes your personal cava config.

  updates come from pacman; the in-shell updater stays out of the way.
  `silere status` reports that ownership instead of offering a second updater.

EOF
}

post_upgrade() {
    cat <<'EOF'

  silere was updated. restart it to pick up the new version:
    silere restart

  panels load when first opened, so one opened before that restart can
  fail against the old version still running.

EOF
}

post_remove() {
    cat <<'EOF'

  silere is removed. two things it was wired into are left in your home
  directory, because pacman does not own them:

    the autostart line you added to your compositor config
      (the hl.exec_cmd line in hyprland.lua, or niri's `spawn-at-startup`)

    matugen, if you ran --repair-matugen: the block marked
      `# silere-shell begin` in ~/.config/matugen/config.toml, plus
      ~/.config/matugen/templates/silere-shell/ and
      ~/.config/matugen/silere-shell.json

  settings stay in ~/.config/silere-shell and notification history in
  ~/.local/state/silere-shell, in case you come back.

EOF
}
